"Speed limits, connections per torrent, upload slots and seeding are set for each torrent when you add it, or later under Torrent Settings. Torrents use the proxy from the Connection tab (HTTP or SOCKS5, or the Mac's proxy with \"Use the system settings\") and the speed limit for all downloads. Changes apply to torrents started afterwards. Peers and trackers can see your IP address, or your proxy's." = "Hoʻonohonohoʻia nā palena wikiwiki, nā pilina i kēlā me kēia torrent, nā slot hoʻouka a me ka hānai no kēlā me kēia torrent ke hoʻohuiʻoe iā ia, a iʻole ma hope aku ma lalo o nā Hoʻonohonoho Torrent. Hoʻohana nā torrents i ka hoaaloha mai ka papa kuhikuhi Hoʻopili (HTTP a iʻole SOCKS5, a iʻole ka hoaaloha o ka Mac me \"Hoʻohana i nā hoʻonohonoho o ka pūnaha\") a me ka palena wikiwiki no nā kaohi āpau. E hoʻohana nā hoʻololi i nā torrents i hoʻomakaʻia ma hope. Hiki i nā hoaaloha a me nā trackers ke ʻike i kāu wahi IP, a i ʻole kāu hoaaloha.";
"Settings used for every download from a website. A site also covers its subdomains (example.com covers www.example.com). Logins are only sent to that site and are kept with the app's other secrets." = "Nā hoʻonohonoho i hoʻohana ʻia no kēlā me kēia hoʻoiho mai i kahi pūnaewele. Hoʻopili pū kekahi pūnaewele i kāna mau wahi ʻōpio (hoʻopili ʻo example.com i www.example.com). Hoʻouna wale ʻia nā hoʻokomo i kēlā pūnaewele a mālama ʻia me nā ʻōlelo huna ʻē aʻe o ka noi.";
"A backup holds your settings, site settings, queues and the downloads list. Passwords and cookies are never put in a backup." = "Hoʻopaʻa ʻia kāu hoʻonohonoho, nā hoʻonohonoho pūnaewele, nā kāhea a me ka papa inoa o nā kāhea. ʻAʻole i waiho ʻia nā kīwī a me nā kīwī i loko o ka hoʻopaʻa ʻana.";
"When you copy a link that ends in one of these types, the Add window opens with it." = "Inā kope ʻoe i kahi loulou e pau ana i kekahi o kēia mau ʻano, e wehe ʻia ka ʻaoʻao Hoʻohui me ia.";
"Expected checksums are checked automatically when a download finishes. Queues can also quit the app, sleep or shut down the Mac when they are done (Scheduler)." = "Hoʻāʻo ʻia nā checksums i manaʻo ʻia i ka wā e pau ai ka hoʻouka ʻana. Hiki iā Queues ke haʻalele i ka noi, hoʻomaha, a i ʻole hoʻopau i ka Mac i ka wā i hana ʻia ai lākou (Scheduler).";
"Save the extension folder, open the browser's extensions page, switch on Developer mode, choose Load unpacked and pick the folder." = "Hoʻouna i ka papa kuhikuhi hoʻohui, e wehe i ka ʻaoʻao hoʻohui o ka mea huli, e hoʻololi i ka mode Developer, e koho i ka Load unpacked a koho i ka papa kuhikuhi.";
"Save the add-on file and drag it onto a Firefox window. Firefox installs add-ons that are signed; see the README for signing your copy." = "Hoʻouna i ka faila hoʻohui a kāwili iā ia i loko o kahi window Firefox. Hoʻonohonoho ʻo Firefox i nā hoʻohui i hoʻopaʻa inoa ʻia; e ʻike i ka README no ka hoʻopaʻa inoa ʻana i kāu kope.";
"Install the ndm command, then for example: ndm https://example.com/file.zip --queue Night" = "Hoʻokomo i ka'ōlelo aʻoaʻo ndm, a laila no ka laʻana: ndm https://example.com/file.zip --queue Night";
"Finding the qualities on offer…" = "E ʻimi i nā ʻano i hāʻawi ʻia…";
"Video sites are saved in the best quality available, with picture and sound joined." = "Hoʻouna ʻia nā pūnaewele wikiō i ka maikaʻi maikaʻi loa, me ka kiʻi a me ka leo i hui pū ʻia.";
"Put a range in square brackets: [001-100] keeps three digits, [1-100] does not, [a-z] uses letters and [0-100:5] counts in fives. Several ranges multiply." = "E kau i kahi papa i loko o nā kāpili: [001-100] e mālama ana i ʻekolu mau helu, [1-100] ʻaʻole, [a-z] e hoʻohana ana i nā huaʻōlelo a me [0-100:5] e helu ana i nā lima. He nui nā papa i ka hoʻololi ʻana.";
"Explores a website section and lists the files it links to. Only use it on sites you are allowed to download from." = "E hōʻiliʻili ana i kahi ʻāpana pūnaewele a hōʻike i nā faila i hoʻopilikia ʻia. E hoʻohana wale i kēia ma nā pūnaewele i loaʻa iā ʻoe ka ʻae e hoʻouka mai ai.";
